{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116430",
      "title": "Link Shortcuts & Programmatic Navigation",
      "lectureOrder": 281,
      "videoOrder": 268,
      "sourceHash": "5b73ea4b8d7ce4153e15ac25d2a98bc2ad96f9cee8ff3b3d57c300fa7a3e31c7",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 4.11,
          "en": "So, to allow users to add new tasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.11,
          "end": 7.65,
          "en": "we should go to this new task component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.65,
          "end": 12.06,
          "en": "And in there you already find quite a lot of code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.06,
          "end": 16.74,
          "en": "I already have some signals in there which are connected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.74,
          "end": 20.763,
          "en": "to a forum and it's inputs with help of two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 22.29,
          "end": 24.81,
          "en": "And then in on submit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.81,
          "end": 28.92,
          "en": "I'm calling add task in a task service, which is a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.92,
          "end": 30.843,
          "en": "that will create a new task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.04,
          "end": 34.62,
          "en": "So that's all already here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.62,
          "end": 38.88,
          "en": "I also already expect the user ID as an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.88,
          "end": 43.65,
          "en": "and since we did enable this strategy here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 43.65,
          "end": 46.38,
          "en": "which ensures that child routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.38,
          "end": 49.637,
          "en": "do get dynamic path parameter values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.637,
          "end": 53.55,
          "en": "as inputs by Angular, since we did that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.55,
          "end": 56.67,
          "en": "this user ID will be set here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 56.67,
          "end": 59.46,
          "en": "So that will be extracted from the path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.46,
          "end": 60.88,
          "en": "that's currently active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.04,
          "end": 64.98,
          "en": "and therefore this should all already work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.98,
          "end": 68.253,
          "en": "and adding tasks should therefore already work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 69.84,
          "end": 72.45,
          "en": "And indeed you can give this a try.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.45,
          "end": 77.193,
          "en": "If you go back and you enter some task data here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 78.24,
          "end": 82.11,
          "en": "if you click create and you then go to a different user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 82.11,
          "end": 86.643,
          "en": "and come back to this user, you should see that task here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 88.2,
          "end": 90.503,
          "en": "And it should also be there if you reload the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 90.503,
          "end": 93.66,
          "en": "because it's getting stored in local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 93.66,
          "end": 95.643,
          "en": "That's all already working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 96.99000000000001,
          "end": 98.819,
          "en": "But of course it would be nice if",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 98.819,
          "end": 103.56,
          "en": "after clicking create we would automatically be navigated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 103.56,
          "end": 106.38,
          "en": "to this task view here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 106.38,
          "end": 109.32,
          "en": "And the same should be true if you click cancel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 109.32,
          "end": 114.3,
          "en": "There, I also wanna be able to go back to that tasks view.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 114.3,
          "end": 117.9,
          "en": "And I will start with the cancel button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 117.9,
          "end": 121.26,
          "en": "because that actually is already a link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 121.26,
          "end": 123.9,
          "en": "And therefore if you want to go back, all we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 123.9,
          "end": 128.403,
          "en": "to do is add a router link and set the appropriate path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 129.6,
          "end": 133.86,
          "en": "And here the path can be dot slash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 133.86,
          "end": 138.21,
          "en": "that's a special router link syntax supported by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 138.21,
          "end": 140.777,
          "en": "which essentially tells it that you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 140.777,
          "end": 145.14,
          "en": "to go up one level in your route path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 145.14,
          "end": 148.44,
          "en": "It will essentially remove the last segment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 148.44,
          "end": 150.39,
          "en": "of your route path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 150.39,
          "end": 155.28,
          "en": "So if you are on users, u3 tasks new,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 155.28,
          "end": 159.663,
          "en": "this will get you to users u3 tasks for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 161.22,
          "end": 164.4,
          "en": "So that's a nice little feature offered by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 164.4,
          "end": 167.433,
          "en": "to simplify relative navigations like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 169.56,
          "end": 172.38,
          "en": "So that's the cancel button working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 172.38,
          "end": 175.497,
          "en": "What about the create button though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 175.497,
          "end": 180.497,
          "en": "That is a real button because it indeed needs to be a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 180.57,
          "end": 182.355,
          "en": "because it submits the form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 182.355,
          "end": 185.97,
          "en": "and it triggers on submit therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 185.97,
          "end": 188.55,
          "en": "So here we have a new use case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 188.55,
          "end": 193.17,
          "en": "We now need to perform programmatic navigation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 193.17,
          "end": 196.41,
          "en": "which means we don't want to navigate with help of a link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 196.41,
          "end": 199.817,
          "en": "but instead we want to trigger a navigation action from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 199.817,
          "end": 201.903,
          "en": "inside our code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 202.77,
          "end": 204.9,
          "en": "And that's also a common requirement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 204.9,
          "end": 208.29,
          "en": "and therefore something that's supported by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 208.29,
          "end": 210.073,
          "en": "So therefore, all you need to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 210.073,
          "end": 214.254,
          "en": "to navigate programmatically is inject a router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 214.254,
          "end": 219.09,
          "en": "service, which is offered by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 219.09,
          "end": 222.19,
          "en": "So the thing you inject is just called router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 223.32,
          "end": 226.503,
          "en": "and that is imported from @Angular router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 227.454,
          "end": 230.57999999999998,
          "en": "And with that injected, you can go to the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 230.57999999999998,
          "end": 233.43,
          "en": "where you want to trigger that navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 233.43,
          "end": 236.394,
          "en": "So here in this case, the end of on submit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 236.394,
          "end": 240.314,
          "en": "and call this router, navigate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 240.314,
          "end": 242.64,
          "en": "to guess what?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 242.64,
          "end": 243.483,
          "en": "Navigate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 244.98,
          "end": 246.658,
          "en": "Router also has some other",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 246.658,
          "end": 250.02,
          "en": "methods and properties you can use to interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 250.02,
          "end": 251.4,
          "en": "with the router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 251.4,
          "end": 255.93,
          "en": "but Navigate is one of the most commonly used methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 255.93,
          "end": 260.43,
          "en": "because Navigate then takes your navigation commands",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 260.43,
          "end": 263.79,
          "en": "and then possibly some extra configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 263.79,
          "end": 267.57,
          "en": "And therefore here I'll pass an array to navigate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 267.57,
          "end": 270.42,
          "en": "because these navigation commands, which it wants,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 270.42,
          "end": 271.984,
          "en": "should be an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 271.984,
          "end": 275.46,
          "en": "And this array is the same kind of array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 275.46,
          "end": 277.89,
          "en": "you could also pass to router link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 277.89,
          "end": 280.86,
          "en": "where you can specify your different segments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 280.86,
          "end": 282.033,
          "en": "like this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 284.01,
          "end": 285.57,
          "en": "In this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 285.57,
          "end": 290.01,
          "en": "I want to navigate to slash users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 290.01,
          "end": 295.01,
          "en": "then the current user id and then tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 295.59000000000003,
          "end": 298.83299999999997,
          "en": "That's how we could construct our array here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 300.54,
          "end": 303.6,
          "en": "And then you can also pass a configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 303.6,
          "end": 308.25,
          "en": "to navigate and configure various things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 308.25,
          "end": 311.37,
          "en": "For example, you could also add query parameters if you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 311.37,
          "end": 313.98,
          "en": "needed to, but you can also, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 313.98,
          "end": 317.212,
          "en": "set replace URL to true to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 317.212,
          "end": 320.82,
          "en": "that this navigation action essentially works like a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 320.82,
          "end": 325.08,
          "en": "redirect and ensures that the user can't use the back button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 325.08,
          "end": 328.173,
          "en": "to go back to this page where they're coming from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 329.01,
          "end": 331.26,
          "en": "Because sometimes you want to disable that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 331.26,
          "end": 334.47,
          "en": "especially after a form has been submitted so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 334.47,
          "end": 336.69,
          "en": "that if the user clicks back thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 336.69,
          "end": 340.773,
          "en": "they're not taken back to this new task component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 341.94,
          "end": 345.06,
          "en": "So here for demo purposes, I will set that to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 345.06,
          "end": 349.40999999999997,
          "en": "And with all that, if you save that and you go to a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 349.40999999999997,
          "end": 351.1,
          "en": "and add a new task",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 355.14,
          "end": 357.39,
          "en": "like this and you click create,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 357.39,
          "end": 362.37,
          "en": "you see I'm automatically navigated to this user tasks page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 362.37,
          "end": 367.05,
          "en": "And if I now would use that back button, you see I am taken",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 367.05,
          "end": 370.74,
          "en": "to some other pages, but not to that new task page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 370.74,
          "end": 373.263,
          "en": "That's what replace URL does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 374.79,
          "end": 379.77,
          "en": "Now with that, we added all the task related functionality.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 379.77,
          "end": 382.86,
          "en": "We can view the tasks, we can add tasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 382.86,
          "end": 385.89,
          "en": "and this complete button also should already work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 385.89,
          "end": 388.473,
          "en": "because that has nothing to do with routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 389.58,
          "end": 393.03,
          "en": "But there still are more routing related features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 393.03,
          "end": 394.593,
          "en": "which we'll explore next.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
